.TH UDPREFLECTOR 1 "July 17, 2026" "udpreflector" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
udpreflector \- relay UDP packets between recently active endpoints
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B udpreflector
.BI --port-start= port
.BI --port-end= port
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B udpreflector
listens on an inclusive range of IPv4 and IPv6 UDP ports, learns remote
endpoints from received packets, and forwards each accepted packet unchanged
to the other recently active endpoints on the same logical port.
.PP
Configuration is supplied through command-line options and remains fixed for
the lifetime of the process.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --version
Print the build identifier and exit without opening listeners.
.TP
.BI --port-start= port
First UDP port in the required inclusive range.
.TP
.BI --port-end= port
Last UDP port in the required inclusive range.
.TP
.BI --peer-timeout= duration
Peer inactivity timeout. The default is 1m.
.TP
.BI --max-peers-per-port= count
Maximum active peers per logical UDP port. The default is 256.
.TP
.BI --udp4-address= address
IPv4 listening address. The default is 0.0.0.0.
.TP
.BI --udp6-address= address
IPv6 listening address. The default is ::.
.TP
.BI --metrics-address= host:port
Enable Prometheus metrics on this HTTP listening address. Metrics are disabled
when this option is omitted.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/udpreflector.service
Example hardened systemd service using UDP ports 40000 through 40100.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR systemd.service (5)
